<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humbert II of Viennois</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1312–1355</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Humbert II of Viennois was the last independent Dauphin of the Viennois, ruling from 1333. He founded a university at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenoble">Grenoble</a> in 1339 and led a papal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> to Smyrna in 1345 to 1347. Heavily in debt and without an heir, he sold the Dauphiné to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1349; it passed to the king's eldest son, who thereafter bore the title Dauphin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/humbert-ii-of-viennois.jpg" alt="Humbert II of Viennois" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown beginning of XVIIth · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dauphin_Humbert_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
